---
title: "create_user POST /v1/integration/user (Legion Backend API)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_auth: api_key = headers["x-api-key"]
    q_auth --> q_check_key: api_key != null
    q_check_key --> q_sign: signature = HMAC_SHA256(secret_key, body)
    q_check_key --> q_reject_key: api_key == null or invalid
    q_reject_key --> [*]: revert "unauthorized"
    q_sign --> q_attach_sig: set_header("X-Signature", signature)
    q_attach_sig --> q_send: POST /v1/integration/user with body
    q_send --> q_validate_resp: response = server_response
    q_validate_resp --> q_success: response.status == 2xx
    q_validate_resp --> q_error: response.status != 2xx
    q_success --> [*]: return user_record
    q_error --> [*]: revert "user creation failed"

    note right of q_auth
        INV-001: x-api-key header is required on every request
        INV-002: request body must be signed with HMAC-SHA256 before sending
        INV-003: user creation is idempotent or returns error on duplicate
    end note
